# Firebase Crashlytics

Package:

* `@react-native-firebase/crashlytics`

## Current project status

Crashlytics is installed and configured through the native plugin.

There is currently no manual Crashlytics instrumentation in application JS/TS code.

The native SDK may automatically report production crashes when Firebase and Crashlytics are correctly initialized.

## Rules

* Do NOT add manual Crashlytics reporting unless explicitly requested.
* Do NOT add `crashlytics().recordError()` to every catch block automatically.
* Do NOT use Crashlytics as general-purpose application logging.
* Do NOT add breadcrumbs or custom logs unless they provide useful diagnostic information.
* Do NOT modify Crashlytics configuration as part of an unrelated task.
* Never send passwords, tokens, authentication credentials, secrets, or private user content to Crashlytics.
* Avoid recording expected/normal application errors as Crashlytics errors.
* Prefer recording unexpected, actionable production failures.

## Error handling

Normal expected errors should be handled by the application normally.

Only use Crashlytics when the error is important for diagnosing a real production problem.

Do not replace existing error handling merely to add Crashlytics reporting.
